WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.710
The polymer in a plastic bag
is built from just one kind of

2
00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:06.910
small molecule, joined
over and over again,

3
00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.230
and nothing else comes out.

4
00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:10.890
Polyester is different.

5
00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:13.570
Every time two of its
building blocks link up,

6
00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:16.530
a small molecule of
water is given off.

7
00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:19.070
So why do some polymers
throw out a by-product,

8
00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:21.090
while others do not?

9
00:00:21.140 --> 00:00:24.690
In this mission, you'll open up
the double bond in an alkene to

10
00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:27.650
build an addition polymer,
and draw its repeat unit.

11
00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:31.590
Then you'll join monomers that
have two reactive groups each,

12
00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:34.810
and watch a condensation polymer form.

13
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:39.070
Your mission: explain why only
some polymers give off water.
